COG END USER LICENCE AGREEMENT (EULA)
=====================================

Version: 0.2-draft (2026-06-08)
Status:  DRAFT pending review by qualified legal counsel.
         Do not rely on this document as a final agreement. It is
         intended as a starting point for solicitor review.

Copyright (c) 2026 Grey & Associates Ltd ("Licensor"). All rights
reserved.

This document is the End User Licence Agreement for the Cog
software product ("Cog"). It governs your use of the Cog binary
installed on hardware you control. Use of any hosted services
operated by the Licensor at getcog.ai (or any subdomain thereof)
is governed by the separate Terms of Service published at
https://getcog.ai/terms-of-service, not by this EULA.

This document supersedes any previous LICENCE file shipped with
Cog. Prior MIT-licensed revisions of the Cog source remain
governed by the historical notice at docs/LEGACY_MIT_NOTICE.md and
continue to apply to those revisions; that grant does not extend
to this or any subsequent revision.


1. DEFINITIONS
--------------

  "Cog" means the executable binary distributed by the Licensor
  under the name Cog, together with any libraries, schemas,
  configuration files, scripts, and documentation provided
  alongside it.

  "You" or "Licensee" means the individual or legal entity
  exercising the rights granted under this EULA. Where you are an
  individual acting on behalf of an organisation, "you" includes
  that organisation and you warrant that you are authorised to
  bind it.

  "Licence" means the rights granted under this EULA.

  "Tier" means one of the four product tiers Cog ships in: Free,
  Pro, Family, and Teams. Each Tier has distinct usage scope
  defined in Schedule A.

  "Licence File" means the Ed25519-signed file issued by the
  Licensor that authorises operation of the Cog binary at a Tier
  other than Free.

  "Seat" means one authenticated user account permitted by a
  Tier's seat count.


2. GRANT OF LICENCE
-------------------

  2.1  Free Tier (perpetual). Subject to the restrictions in
       section 3, the Licensor grants you a perpetual,
       non-exclusive, non-transferable, single-Seat, royalty-free
       Licence to install and operate Cog on hardware you control,
       provided that no Licence File is present at startup. Running
       Cog in this configuration constitutes acceptance of the
       Free Tier terms in Schedule A.

  2.2  Paid Tiers (Pro, Family, Teams). Subject to a valid Licence
       File issued by the Licensor and ongoing payment of the
       applicable subscription fees, the Licensor grants you a
       non-exclusive, non-transferable, time-limited Licence to
       install and operate Cog at the corresponding Tier on
       hardware you control. The Licence terminates automatically
       upon expiry of the Licence File or non-payment of fees,
       whereupon the binary continues to operate under the Free
       Tier (subject to section 2.1).

  2.3  Developer / Internal Tier. The "dev" Licence type is a
       30-day loopback-only Licence intended exclusively for
       internal evaluation. It is not valid for production
       deployment and the binary will refuse to bind a non-
       loopback address while operating under it.

  2.4  Updates and upgrades. Where you hold a paid-Tier Licence,
       the Licensor may make updates available to you at no
       additional cost. Updates are part of Cog and subject to
       this EULA. The Licensor has no obligation to provide
       updates and no obligation to maintain backwards
       compatibility with prior versions.


3. RESTRICTIONS
---------------

  Without the prior written consent of the Licensor, you may NOT:

  3.1  Distribute, publish, sublicence, sell, lease, rent, lend,
       or otherwise transfer Cog or any portion thereof to any
       third party;

  3.2  Reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, or otherwise
       attempt to derive the source code, algorithms, or trade
       secrets of Cog, except (a) to the limited extent expressly
       permitted by the Software Directive (Directive 2009/24/EC)
       and the Copyright, Designs and Patents Act 1988 for
       interoperability purposes, or (b) where such restriction
       is otherwise prohibited by mandatory applicable law;

  3.3  Use Cog to develop, market, operate, or assist any third
       party in developing, marketing, or operating a product or
       service that competes with Cog as defined in section 8
       (Trademark and Competing Use);

  3.4  Remove, alter, obscure, or interfere with any copyright,
       trademark, licence, or other proprietary notice, label, or
       Licence enforcement mechanism present in Cog;

  3.5  Use Cog beyond the scope authorised by the Tier you hold,
       including but not limited to exceeding the permitted Seat
       count, custom-gear quota, custom-agent quota, or
       communication-channel set defined in Schedule A;

  3.6  Use Cog in any application or environment requiring
       fail-safe performance or where failure could lead to
       death, personal injury, or environmental damage, including
       but not limited to operation of nuclear facilities, life
       support systems, or air traffic control;

  3.7  Use Cog in violation of applicable export-control laws,
       sanctions regimes (including but not limited to those
       administered by HM Treasury, OFAC, the EU, and the United
       Nations), or other applicable law.


4. PROVIDER KEYS AND THIRD-PARTY COSTS
--------------------------------------

  Cog is a BYO-key system. You contract directly with model
  providers (such as Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, DeepSeek, xAI,
  Qwen, Moonshot, or others) and you are solely responsible for
  all costs incurred against your provider accounts. The
  Licensor is not a party to your relationship with any model
  provider and has no liability for charges, suspensions, rate
  limits, or other actions taken by such providers in respect of
  your account.

  Cog's cost-telemetry feature is a best-effort estimate. The
  authoritative source of charges is each provider's own
  invoicing.


5. PAID-TIER LICENCE FILES
--------------------------

  5.1  Issuance. Paid-Tier Licence Files are issued by the
       Licensor following completion of the corresponding
       subscription process. Issuance details (delivery method,
       bound metadata) are described in the Terms of Service.

  5.2  Verification. Licence verification is performed locally
       against an embedded public key. Cog does not transmit
       Licence data to the Licensor or any third party. The
       Licensor has no telemetry on Cog's operation under any
       Tier.

  5.3  Expiry. Paid-Tier Licence Files carry an expiry timestamp.
       Cog issues a soft-warning beginning 30 days before
       expiry. Upon expiry, paid-Tier features become unavailable
       and Cog falls back to Free Tier operation per section 2.2.

  5.4  No phone-home. Air-gapped operation is supported at every
       Tier.


