----------------------

  TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, COG IS
  PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE," WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY
  KIND, EXPRESS, IMPLIED, OR STATUTORY, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED
  TO THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A
  PARTICULAR PURPOSE, NON-INFRINGEMENT, AND ABSENCE OF DEFECTS.

  The Licensor does not warrant that Cog will be uninterrupted,
  error-free, secure against intrusion, or that defects will be
  corrected. The Licensor does not warrant that Cog's output is
  accurate, complete, reliable, or fit for any particular
  purpose; Cog dispatches to third-party model providers whose
  output is outside the Licensor's control.

  Nothing in this section limits or excludes any warranty,
  guarantee, or other right that cannot be limited or excluded
  under applicable law, including statutory rights of consumers
  under the UK Consumer Rights Act 2015.


7. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY
--------------------------

  7.1  Excluded losses. TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY
       APPLICABLE LAW, IN NO EVENT SHALL THE LICENSOR BE LIABLE
       FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, EXEMPLARY,
       CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR FOR LOSS OF
       PROFITS, REVENUE, GOODWILL, DATA, OR ANTICIPATED SAVINGS,
       ARISING OUT OF OR RELATED TO YOUR USE OF OR INABILITY TO
       USE COG, EVEN IF THE LICENSOR HAS BEEN ADVISED OF THE
       POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.

  7.2  Cap on direct damages. The aggregate liability of the
       Licensor arising out of or relating to this EULA, whether
       in contract, tort, or otherwise, shall not exceed:
       (a) for the Free Tier, £100 (one hundred pounds sterling);
       (b) for paid Tiers, the total subscription fees paid by
       you to the Licensor in the twelve (12) months immediately
       preceding the event giving rise to the claim.

  7.3  Carve-outs. Nothing in this section limits or excludes
       liability for: (a) death or personal injury caused by the
       Licensor's negligence; (b) fraud or fraudulent
       misrepresentation; (c) any other liability that cannot be
       limited or excluded under applicable law.


8. TRADEMARK AND COMPETING USE
------------------------------

  8.1  Trademarks. "Cog," the Cog logo, and any other names,
       marks, and brand elements used in connection with Cog are
       trademarks of the Licensor. This EULA does not grant you
       any right to use those marks except as required for fair
       descriptive use under applicable law.

  8.2  Compatible gear authoring. Notwithstanding section 3.3,
       you may publish, distribute, and identify gear declarations,
       editor extensions, validators, and similar third-party
       tools as "compatible with Cog" or equivalent factual
       descriptive language, provided that:
       (a) such use is truthful and not misleading;
       (b) such use does not imply endorsement, sponsorship, or
       affiliation with the Licensor; and
       (c) such use does not incorporate the Cog logo or other
       design marks without prior written consent.

  8.3  Competing use. "Competing product or service" in
       section 3.3 means a product or service that performs
       substantially the same function as Cog (operating an AI
       agent loop with typed in-process tool dispatch and a
       Postgres-backed trace store) and is offered to third
       parties in commerce. Authoring gear declarations against
       the public schema published at
       https://github.com/GreyAssoc/cogai is not a competing use.


9. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY
------------------------

  All title, ownership rights, and intellectual property rights
  in and to Cog, including all copies and derivative works of
  Cog, remain with the Licensor and its licensors. This EULA
  grants you no ownership rights in or to Cog. Where you create
  custom gears, agents, or configurations through Cog, the
  Licensor claims no ownership of those work-products; you
  retain ownership subject to the Licensor's underlying rights
  in Cog.


10. CONFIDENTIALITY (PAID TIERS)
--------------------------------

  Paid-Tier Licence Files and any associated Licence-issuance
  metadata are confidential information of the Licensor. You
  agree to protect such information with at least the same
  degree of care that you use to protect your own confidential
  information of similar importance, but in no event less than
  reasonable care, and not to disclose it to any third party
  except as required by applicable law.


11. TERM AND TERMINATION
------------------------

  11.1 Term. The Free-Tier Licence is perpetual subject to
       sections 3 and 11.2. Paid-Tier Licences are co-terminus
       with the corresponding subscription period.

  11.2 Termination for breach. The Licensor may terminate this
       EULA upon written notice if you materially breach it and
       (where the breach is curable) fail to cure the breach
       within thirty (30) days after receipt of notice
       describing the breach.

  11.3 Effect of termination. Upon termination, all rights
       granted under this EULA cease and you must cease all use
       of Cog and destroy all copies of Cog in your possession or
       control. Sections 6, 7, 8.1, 9, 10, 12, 13, and 14
       survive termination.


12. EXPORT CONTROLS AND SANCTIONS
---------------------------------

  You acknowledge that Cog may be subject to export-control laws
  and economic sanctions regimes. You agree not to install,
  export, re-export, transfer, or use Cog in any manner that
  violates such laws, including but not limited to (a) export
  to any country, person, or entity subject to comprehensive
  sanctions administered by HM Treasury, OFAC, the EU, or the
  United Nations, or (b) use by any person or entity on a
  denied-party list.


13. GOVERNING LAW AND JURISDICTION
----------------------------------

  This EULA is governed by and construed in accordance with the
  laws of England and Wales, without regard to conflict-of-laws
  principles. The courts of England and Wales shall have
  exclusive jurisdiction to settle any dispute or claim arising
  out of or in connection with this EULA, save that the Licensor
  may bring proceedings against you in any jurisdiction where
  you operate or are domiciled to enforce or protect its
  intellectual property rights.


14. GENERAL
-----------

  14.1 Entire agreement. This EULA, together with any Licence
       File and (where applicable) the Terms of Service,
       constitutes the entire agreement between you and the
       Licensor regarding Cog and supersedes all prior or
       contemporaneous agreements, representations, warranties,
       and understandings.

  14.2 Severability. If any provision of this EULA is held to
       be unenforceable, the remaining provisions remain in
       full force and the unenforceable provision shall be
       construed to give the maximum effect permitted by law.

  14.3 Waiver. No failure or delay by the Licensor in exercising
       any right shall operate as a waiver of that right.

  14.4 Assignment. You may not assign this EULA without the
       Licensor's prior written consent. The Licensor may
       assign this EULA without restriction.

  14.5 Force majeure. Neither party is liable for any failure
       or delay in performance to the extent caused by
       circumstances beyond its reasonable control.

  14.6 Notices. Notices to the Licensor shall be sent to
       legal@getcog.ai. Notices to you may be given by email
       to any address you have provided to the Licensor or by
       posting to https://getcog.ai/notices.

  14.7 No third-party beneficiaries. A person who is not a
       party to this EULA has no rights under the Contracts
       (Rights of Third Parties) Act 1999 to enforce any term.

  14.8 Amendment. The Licensor may amend this EULA from time
       to time. Continued use of Cog after the effective date
       of any amendment constitutes acceptance of the amended
       EULA. Material changes affecting paid-Tier rights will
       not take effect for existing paid-Tier subscribers until
       their current subscription period ends.


SCHEDULE A — TIER MATRIX
========================

The Tier-specific entitlements are defined in the canonical Tier
specification at TIERS.md, which forms part of this EULA. The
matrix below is a summary; in case of conflict between this
summary and TIERS.md, TIERS.md governs.

  Free Tier
    Seats:                1
    Custom gears:         3 above Tier 0 baseline
    Custom agents:        3 beyond built-ins
    Communication:        Telegram + Discord
    Trace retention:      30 days
    Licence:              No licence file required
    Subscription:         None

  Pro Tier
    Seats:                1
    Custom gears:         Unlimited
    Custom agents:        Unlimited
    Communication:        Telegram + Discord + WhatsApp +
                          web chat + HTTP API + IDE/CLI
    Trace retention:      365 days
    Licence:              Required
    Subscription:         Required

  Family Tier
    Seats:                Up to 4 (1 parent + 3 children)
    Custom gears:         3 per Seat (12 total)
    Custom agents:        3 per Seat
    Communication:        Telegram + Discord + WhatsApp + web chat
    Trace retention:      365 days
    Licence:              Required
    Subscription:         Required

  Teams Tier
    Seats:                Unlimited
    Custom gears:         Unlimited
    Custom agents:        Unlimited
    Communication:        All + on-prem connector
    Trace retention:      Configurable
    Licence:              Required, bound to organisation and
                          Seat count
    Subscription:         Required

The "dev" Licence is documented separately and is not a
commercial Tier.


